---
description: Recall durable project memory and session continuity with WhiteMagic before answering state questions; prefer explicit wm routes.
alwaysApply: false
---

When this project uses WhiteMagic (the local MCP server):

- Before answering "what do we know / what was decided / where were we", call
  `session_continuity` (or on Gen 2 `v9.3.4` fallback: `wm(route="session.continuity", args={"n": 5})`).
- Search durable memory with `memory_recall(query="...")` (Gen 2: `wm(route="memory.search", args={"query": "..."})`).
- Persist decisions with
  `memory_remember(content="...", importance=0.8, tags=["decision"])` (Gen 2: `wm(route="memory.create", args=...)`) and record checkpoints with `session_checkpoint`.
- `wm` remains available alongside the 19 `cyberbrain` MCP tools for explicit route dispatch.
- All memory stays local by default; never send memory content to third-party
  services.
